+some \(n\) with \(t<\tau_n(\omega)\), so the stopped-indicator process agrees
+with \(N_t(\omega)\).  Hence \(N_t=0\) almost surely.  If \(t=0\), the claim
+is exactly the normalization \(N_0=0\).
